    <header>
        <h1>JavaScript Backend Course: Master Server-Side Development with JavaScript</h1>
    </header>

    <section>
        <p>Backend development powers modern web and mobile applications. While the frontend handles user interactions, the backend processes data, manages business logic, and keeps applications running smoothly. Learning backend development in <strong>JavaScript</strong> can open doors to high-paying tech roles, especially in startups, SaaS, and large-scale systems.</p>
        <p>A <strong>JavaScript Backend Course</strong> equips you with the skills to design, build, and maintain robust server-side applications.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Why Learn JavaScript for Backend Development?</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Scalability</strong> – Perfect for real-time apps like chat, e-commerce, and social platforms.</li>
            <li><strong>Cross-Platform</strong> – Runs on any OS with Node.js.</li>
            <li><strong>High Performance</strong> – Handles multiple requests efficiently using event-driven architecture.</li>
            <li><strong>Strong Ecosystem</strong> – Frameworks like Express.js, Nest.js, and libraries simplify backend development.</li>
            <li><strong>Community Support</strong> – Large global community and npm packages.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>What You’ll Learn in a JavaScript Backend Course</h2>
        <h3>1. Core JavaScript for Backend</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>ES6+ features: arrow functions, template literals, destructuring.</li>
            <li>Asynchronous programming: callbacks, promises, async/await.</li>
            <li>Objects, arrays, and functional programming basics.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2. Node.js Fundamentals</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Setting up Node.js and npm.</li>
            <li>Event-driven architecture and non-blocking I/O.</li>
            <li>Creating your first server and handling HTTP requests.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>3. Frameworks & Tools</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Express.js</strong> – Routing, middleware, and API handling.</li>
            <li><strong>Nest.js</strong> – Structured framework for scalable apps.</li>
            <li><strong>Authentication & Security</strong> – JWT, OAuth2, and input validation.</li>
            <li>Build tools like npm scripts and nodemon.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>4. Database Management</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>NoSQL: MongoDB with Mongoose.</li>
            <li>SQL: MySQL or PostgreSQL.</li>
            <li>Writing optimized queries and data modeling.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>5. Web Services & APIs</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>RESTful API design with Express/Nest.js.</li>
            <li>JSON data handling.</li>
            <li>API testing and versioning.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>6. Advanced Topics</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Real-time applications with Socket.IO.</li>
            <li>Microservices architecture.</li>
            <li>Containerization with Docker.</li>
            <li>Deployment on AWS, Azure, or GCP.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>7. Hands-On Projects</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>E-commerce backend system.</li>
            <li>Task manager or booking apps.</li>
            <li>Real-time chat application.</li>
            <li>Social media REST APIs with authentication.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

