        <h2>FAQs About JavaScript Backend Courses</h2>
        <p><strong>Q1. Do I need prior programming experience?</strong> No. Courses usually start with basics and progress to advanced topics.</p>
        <p><strong>Q2. How long does it take to learn JavaScript backend?</strong> Typically 2–4 months with consistent practice.</p>
        <p><strong>Q3. Is Node.js necessary for backend development?</strong> Yes. It’s the industry standard for modern JavaScript backend development.</p>
        <p><strong>Q4. Can I become a full-stack developer?</strong> Yes. Combine backend knowledge with frontend frameworks like React, Angular, or Vue.</p>
        <p><strong>Q5. Will I work on projects?</strong> Yes. Hands-on projects are included to build your portfolio and practical experience.</p>
